Feature: Masking Invoice Numbers in d_product_revenue_clone Table

  Background:
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone does not exist
    When a replica of the table d_product_revenue is created in d_product_revenue_clone

  Scenario: Mask last four digits of invoice_number for all entries in d_product_revenue_clone
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone is created
    When I retrieve all records from d_product_revenue_clone
    Then I mask the last four digits of the invoice_number column with ****

  Scenario Outline: Verify masking for different invoice_number formats
    Given the invoice_number <invoice_number> in d_product_revenue_clone
    When the masking is applied
    Then the masked invoice_number should be <masked_invoice>

    Examples:
      | invoice_number | masked_invoice |
      | 1234234534     | 123423****     |
      | 9876543210     | 987654****     |
      | 4445556666     | 444555****     |

  Scenario: Error handling when invoice_number format is invalid
    Given an invalid invoice_number of IncorrectFormat in d_product_revenue_clone
    When masking is attempted
    Then an error message "Invalid invoice_number format" should be logged

  Scenario: Checking data preservation after masking
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone with masked entries
    When data in other columns is compared with original table
    Then all other data fields should remain unchanged
